From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Jelonek <jonas@jonasjelonek.de>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:57:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phylink: pass physical media to PCS configuration

Host interface modes do not identify the physical medium. Retain a small
media description in phylink and pass it to PCS configuration, including
passive cable length and an attachment generation for same-profile replug.

Force configuration after SFP setup even when the interface is unchanged.
Deliver media-none directly to the active PCS on removal and detach, even
before link-up, and roll back media state on rejected insertion. A later
PCS receives the current media through normal configuration without a
separate module lifecycle or notification replay API.

Adapt existing PCS callbacks to the extended configuration signature.
Only drivers opting into media configuration receive media-none calls.
Initialize the resolver state before forced configuration on early-down
paths. Keep this API extension local to Realtek kernels.

Signed-off-by: Jonas Jelonek <jonas@jonasjelonek.de>
